- `action(n9)` / missing `precedence(n9, n6)`: Source states "If the PO needs to be reworked, it needs to be created again," but the model omits the feedback edge from `n9` to `action(n6)`, breaking the mandated rework cycle. (SMC3, SMC4, SMC5)
- `branch(b3, XOR)`, `branch(b4, XOR)`, `defines(v3,...)`, `defines(v4,...)`, and corresponding guards: These elements hallucinate exclusive decision points and variables. The source describes straightforward sequential progression ("If the Packing Slip is received, proceed to receive the Invoice..."), containing no conditional choices or additional decision variables in this section. (SMC1, SMC4, SMC6)
- `action(n16)` and `precedence(n15, n17)`: Source dictates "If the Invoice is received, proceed to the Three-way match," yet `action(n16)` is a dangling node with no outgoing precedence. The model incorrectly connects `action(n15)` to `n17` instead, severing the intended invoice-to-match dependency. (SMC3, SMC5)
- `branch(b6, AND)` / missing convergence: The simultaneous funding and mailing steps split at `b6` but lack a `converge` node or synchronized precedence structure before the three-way match, violating the implicit requirement that both parallel tracks complete prior to matching. (SMC4)
- `label(n15, n17, "Invoice Received")`: The label misrepresents the edge semantics; it annotates a transition originating from `n15` (which follows inventory receipt), whereas the source explicitly ties invoice receipt to proceeding to the three-way match. (SMC2, SMC3)

Structural Check
- [S1] STC8 failed: Each action node must have exactly one incoming and one outgoing edge. | Node `n16` has in=1 and out=0. | Node `n9` has in=1 and out=0. | DSL: action(n16,"Receive Invoice"); action(n9,"Rework PO")
- [S2] STC9 failed: Each branch node must have exactly one incoming and at least two outgoing edges. | Node `b3` has in=1 and out=1. | Node `b4` has in=1 and out=1. | Node `b5` has in=1 and out=1. | DSL: branch(b3,XOR); branch(b4,XOR); branch(b5,XOR)
- [S3] STC11 failed: Each variable definition must have a valid range with at least two distinct values. | Variable `v3` has an invalid range `['Packing Slip Received']`. | Variable `v4` has an invalid range `['Inventory Received']`. | Variable `v5` has an invalid range `['Successful Match']`.
- [S4] STC15 failed: Every variable used in a guard must be formally defined. | Guard `v3 = 'Packing Slip Received'` on `b3 -> n14` uses undefined variable `v3`. | Guard `v4 = 'Inventory Received'` on `b4 -> n15` uses undefined variable `v4`. | Guard `v5 = 'Successful Match'` on `b5 -> n18` uses undefined variable `v5`. | DSL: guard(b3,n14,"v3 = 'Packing Slip Received'"); guard(b4,n15,"v4 = 'Inventory Received'"); guard(b5,n18,"v5 = 'Successful Match'")
- [S5] STC20 failed: Every non-end node must have a path to at least one end node. | Violations: b3, n10, n12, n14, n16, n9 | DSL: branch(b3,XOR); action(n10,"Reserve Funds for Released POs"); action(n12,"Receive Packing Slip"); action(n14,"Proceed to Receive Invoice"); action(n16,"Receive Invoice"); action(n9,"Rework PO")

Logical Sanity Check
- [L1] LSC1 failed: Every guard must be satisfiable under the declared ranges of its referenced variables. | Guard `v3 = 'Packing Slip Received'` on `b3 -> n14` cannot be evaluated: `v3` has no declared range. | Guard `v4 = 'Inventory Received'` on `b4 -> n15` cannot be evaluated: `v4` has no declared range. | Guard `v5 = 'Successful Match'` on `b5 -> n18` cannot be evaluated: `v5` has no declared range. | DSL: guard(b3,n14,"v3 = 'Packing Slip Received'"); guard(b4,n15,"v4 = 'Inventory Received'"); guard(b5,n18,"v5 = 'Successful Match'")
- [L2] LSC3 failed: Guards outgoing from XOR/OR branches must cover the whole evaluated state space. | Branch `b3` cannot be evaluated: `v3` has no declared range. | Branch `b4` cannot be evaluated: `v4` has no declared range. | Branch `b5` cannot be evaluated: `v5` has no declared range.
